<!-- 3 SERVICES -->
<section class="light" id="services"><div class="in">
 <p class="eb">What we build and run</p>
 <h2>Seven fence company marketing services, one connected system</h2>
 <p class="lead">A marketing system with seven parts performs at the level of its weakest one. The <a href="/6-gap-revenue-map/">6-Gap Revenue Map™</a> shows which part is leaking most, and we start there, often on the inquiries you already have.</p>
 <div class="tlax" aria-hidden="true"><span>Marketing that brings the inquiry</span><span>Sales systems that sign it</span></div>
 <ol class="tline">
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb1" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="svp1"><span class="tn">01</span><span class="tw">Generate targeted demand</span><span class="th">Google Ads and Local Services Ads</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp1" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb1"><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">01 · Generate targeted demand</p><p>Google Ads and Local Services Ads for fence companies, built by fence type and town, filtered against DIY and "fence panels" shoppers, and paced to the building season. Meta ads and retargeting stay in front of homeowners comparing quotes, and direct mail reaches the streets around every fence you build. <a class="tl" href="/fence-contractor-advertising/">Fence contractor advertising <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> 2–4 weeks, in new quote requests.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp2"><span class="tn">02</span><span class="tw">Build lasting local visibility</span><span class="th">Local SEO and Google Maps</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp2" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb2" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">02 · Build lasting local visibility</p><p>Local SEO for fence companies: "Fence Contractor" as your primary Google Business Profile category, every service listed, then the pages behind the map pack: "privacy fence installation [city]," "vinyl fence company near me," "commercial chain link." Your real competition is the three to five companies serving your zip codes, and that is a winnable fight. <a class="tl" href="/seo-for-fence-companies/">SEO for fence companies <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> 60–90 days to move, 4–6 months to steady calls, then compounds.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp3"><span class="tn">03</span><span class="tw">Own your lead source</span><span class="th">Exclusive leads you own</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp3" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb3" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">03 · Own your lead source</p><p>Exclusive fence leads, generated, not bought: homeowners who contacted you and only you, from a marketing engine you keep. No marketplace selling the same backyard to four other fence companies before you've said hello. <a class="tl" href="/lead-generation-fence-contractors/">Fence lead generation <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> as the mix shifts, with close rates in a different class.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp4"><span class="tn">04</span><span class="tw">Turn research into quote requests</span><span class="th">A website that books the quote</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp4" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb4" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">04 · Turn research into quote requests</p><p>A fence company website built for the phone in a homeowner's hand: galleries by fence type with real photos, license and insurance visible above the fold, a page for each town you serve, a tap-to-call button on every screen and a four- or five-field quote form that says what happens next.</p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> 4–8 weeks, across every channel.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp5"><span class="tn">05</span><span class="tw">Win the comparison</span><span class="th">Reviews and referrals</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp5" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb5" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">05 · Win the comparison</p><p>Every fence you build stands in full view of the neighbors. We make it sell the next one: a review asked for after every install, every review answered, and reviews that name the work ("privacy fence," "vinyl," "pool code") so Google ties you to those searches. <a class="tl" href="/services/reputation-management-for-contractors/">Reputation <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> 2–3 months, then every month after.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp6"><span class="tn">06</span><span class="tw">Convert the inquiries you get</span><span class="th">Speed to lead and quote follow-up</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp6" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb6" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">06 · Convert the inquiries you get</p><p>First contact in minutes, the measure appointment booked and confirmed, the quote delivered while the homeowner is still deciding, then every open quote followed up until it's signed or lost. Fast, fair and followed up beats cheapest more often than fence owners think. It lifts every channel above at once. <a class="tl" href="/services/lead-to-booked-job/">How it works <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> this week, on inquiries you already have.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp7"><span class="tn">07</span><span class="tw">Connect marketing to sold jobs</span><span class="th">Attribution to the sold job</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp7" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb7" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">07 · Connect marketing to sold jobs</p><p>Every call recorded, every form and quote tagged to its source and followed to sold or lost, so each channel's true cost per sold fence decides next month's budget. If something isn't producing jobs, it gets cut and the money moves. <a class="tl" href="/attribution/">How we measure it <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> every month.</p></div></li>
 </ol>
 <p class="tlhint">Tap any step for what it covers.</p>
</div></section>

<!-- 4 MATH: table + calculator -->
<section class="soft" id="math"><div class="in">
 <p class="eb">What the marketing gap costs</p>
 <h2>In fence marketing, the cheapest lead is often your <span class="o">most expensive&nbsp;job.</span></h2>
 <p class="lead">Your marketing report ends at the inquiry. Your business runs on the sold fence, and the two can point in opposite directions.</p>
 <table class="cmp rpt">
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">The report says</th><th scope="col">The decision it drives</th><th scope="col">What's really happening</th><th scope="col">What we'd do</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
   <tr><th scope="row">"We need more leads before&nbsp;spring."</th><td data-l="The decision it drives">Raise the advertising budget.</td><td data-l="What's really happening">Quotes go out days after the call. The homeowner already signed with the first company back.</td><td data-l="What we'd do">Fix response time and quote turnaround first, then decide whether more spend is needed.</td></tr>
   <tr><th scope="row">"Marketplace leads are cheap."</th><td data-l="The decision it drives">Buy more shared leads.</td><td data-l="What's really happening">The same homeowner went to three to five fence companies. You win on price or not at all.</td><td data-l="What we'd do">Compare cost per sold fence by source, then move budget to leads only you receive.</td></tr>
   <tr><th scope="row">"Let's push harder for summer."</th><td data-l="The decision it drives">Spend more in peak season.</td><td data-l="What's really happening">Crews are booked out for weeks. New jobs wait, cancel, or get priced too low to win.</td><td data-l="What we'd do">Weigh crew capacity and margin by fence type. Aim demand at the most profitable work and fill the shoulder&nbsp;months.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
 <div class="calc" id="calc">
  <h3>What one more sold fence in ten quotes is worth</h3>
  <p class="sub">Every marketing vendor sells you cost per lead. Cost per sold fence is the number that decides your budget. Pick a channel, then change the numbers to yours. Nothing you enter is saved.</p>
  <div class="chips" role="group" aria-label="Lead source"><button type="button" data-v="23" aria-pressed="false">Facebook ads · $23</button><button type="button" data-v="50" aria-pressed="true">Google Ads · $50</button><button type="button" data-v="65" aria-pressed="false">Local Services Ads · $65</button></div>
  <div class="cgrid">
   <div class="ins">
    <div><label for="fhCpl">Your cost per lead</label><output id="fhCplOut">$50</output><input type="range" id="fhCpl" min="5" max="300" step="1" value="50"></div>
    <div><label for="fhCr">Inquiries that become sold fences</label><output id="fhCrOut">30%</output><input type="range" id="fhCr" min="1" max="80" step="0.5" value="30"></div>
    <div><label for="fhJob">Average fence install</label><output id="fhJobOut">$3,277</output><input type="range" id="fhJob" min="500" max="25000" step="1" value="3277"></div>
    <div><label for="fhN">Inquiries per month</label><output id="fhNOut">25</output><input type="range" id="fhN" min="5" max="150" step="1" value="25"></div>
   </div>
   <div class="res" aria-live="polite">
    <p class="k">True cost per sold fence</p>
    <p class="big"><span id="fhCpj">$167</span> <small id="fhOne">About 3 in 10 inquiries become a job.</small></p>
    <p class="gp" id="fhPct">5% of a $3,277 average fence.</p>
    <p class="now" id="fhAdd">Ten more points of close rate on the same 25 inquiries a month adds $98,310 a year, with no added ad spend.</p>
   </div>
  </div>
  <details class="how"><summary>Sources and how it's calculated</summary><p>Cost per sold fence = cost per lead ÷ close rate: $50 ÷ 30% = $167. Added revenue = inquiries per month × 10 points × average install × 12: 25 × 10% × $3,277 × 12 = $98,310. Lead costs: Facebook ads $23 per lead (Service Allies), Google Ads $40–60 per lead, Local Services Ads $25–$65 per fencing lead ($71 across home services, The Media Captain, 2025). Average install and 30% close rate are the starting points our fence calculator has always used; project values run from $1,500–$3,000 for chain link to $6,000–$12,000 for privacy and premium fences (HomeGuide, 2026). Marketplace leads go to three to five contractors at once, which is why their close rates sit far below leads you own. Illustration, not a client result. <a href="/free-roi-calculator/">Open the full calculator&nbsp;<span class="ar">→</span></a></p></details>
 </div>
 <p class="midcta"><a class="btn" href="https://calendly.com/andrew-andrewryanmarketing/gap-review?utm_source=arm-site&amp;utm_medium=cta&amp;utm_campaign=site&amp;utm_content=fence-mid">Let's talk about your marketing&nbsp;<span class="ar">→</span></a><span>Bring your real numbers. We'll run them with you.</span></p>
</div></section>

<!-- 5 WHERE JOBS ARE WON OR LOST + GROWTH PATHS -->
<section class="light" id="leaks"><div class="in">
 <p class="eb">Where the job is won or lost</p>
 <h2>Most agencies report the first step. The fence is sold in the last three.</h2>
 <p class="lead">A homeowner buys a fence for privacy, security or the dog, collects three quotes, and usually signs within days. A marketing report that ends at the form fill sees none of that. We follow it to the sold install.</p>
 <ol class="path">
  <li><span class="st">1 · The search</span><b>Found isn't chosen</b><h3>"Privacy fence installation near me"</h3><p>Your ad, map listing or page has to win the click, then the inquiry: a form or a call.</p></li>
  <li><span class="st">2 · The inquiry</span><b>Reached in 5 minutes</b><h3>Before the next fence company calls back</h3><p>The homeowner asked three companies. The first one to reach them usually sets the anchor price.</p></li>
  <li><span class="st">3 · The quote</span><b>Quoted isn't signed</b><h3>Measured, priced,&nbsp;followed&nbsp;up</h3><p>The measure visit, the material choice, the HOA or pool-code question and the follow-up decide it. Most agencies never see this step.</p></li>
  <li><span class="st">4 · The install</span><b>The only number that pays&nbsp;you</b><h3>Signed and installed</h3><p>Crew capacity and material lead times decide how much demand you can use, so marketing never outruns what your crews can build.</p></li>
 </ol>
 <h3 class="h3x">Where should your next million in fence installs come from?</h3>
 <div class="paths3">
  <div><p class="tag">Own your home market</p><h4>You're known in town. The bigger fence company still gets the first call.</h4><p>Take the map pack in your core zip codes, own a high-value niche like ornamental, gates or commercial perimeter work, and answer faster than the big crew can.</p><a class="tl" href="/marketing-for-fence-installers/">See what it takes <span class="ar">→</span></a></div>
  <div><p class="tag">Open the next market</p><h4>New town, no reviews, no referrals.</h4><p>See the cost per installed fence there before you add a crew or a yard. <a href="/contractor-growth-marketing/#readiness">Score your expansion readiness</a> first, free.</p><a class="tl" href="/contractor-growth-marketing/">Model the next market <span class="ar">→</span></a></div>
  <div><p class="tag">Close more of what you quote</p><h4>The quotes go out, but too few sign.</h4><p>Fix the callback, the measure visit and the follow-up before you buy more demand.</p><a class="tl" href="/services/lead-to-booked-job/">Fix the second funnel <span class="ar">→</span></a></div>
 </div>
</div></section>

<!-- 6 PROOF -->
<section class="dark" id="proof"><div class="in">
 <p class="eb">Why trust us with your marketing</p>
 <h2>Our founder built a sales department from scratch. Then made it run without him.</h2>
 <blockquote class="quote"><p>"Andrew was a huge help developing an in-depth marketing system for a window and door business we were working with. His process went way beyond a cookie cutter strategy. He took the time to learn about existing bottlenecks, how to identify new growth opportunities, and measure marketing effectiveness beyond traffic and leads. He even took into account the crew's installation capacity."</p><cite>Gregg Murray, Founder, Relaunch Digital · Verified Google review</cite></blockquote>
 <p class="prov">At a high-volume dealership, Andrew-Ryan Profaci built the Business Development Center (BDC) from nothing: the processes, the follow-up systems, and the tracking from first lead to sold deal. That's the work we do for fence companies. Measure the whole marketing journey, fix what's holding it back, and leave you a marketing system that doesn't need you in every decision.</p>
 <div class="stats s4x"><div><b>11,564</b><span>Leads worked</span></div><div><b>2,135</b><span>Appointments shown</span></div><div><b>761</b><span>Sold</span></div><div><b class="o">35.6%</b><span>Shown appointments sold</span></div></div>
