<!-- 7 ENGAGEMENT -->
<section class="light" id="engagement"><div class="in">
 <p class="eb">How we work with fence companies</p>
 <h2>Three ways to buy fence company marketing. Only one leaves you owning the engine.</h2>
 <table class="cmp">
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">What you're comparing</th><th scope="col">Lead marketplaces</th><th scope="col">A generalist marketing agency</th><th scope="col">Andrew Ryan Marketing</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
   <tr><th scope="row">Who else gets the lead</th><td data-l="Lead marketplaces">Three to five other fence companies, at once.</td><td data-l="A generalist marketing agency">Often another client of theirs in your market.</td><td data-l="Andrew Ryan Marketing">Nobody. One fence company per market, in writing.</td></tr>
   <tr><th scope="row">What gets measured</th><td data-l="Lead marketplaces">Leads delivered.</td><td data-l="A generalist marketing agency">Traffic, rankings, inquiries, and a monthly PDF.</td><td data-l="Andrew Ryan Marketing">Cost per sold fence by channel, every month.</td></tr>
   <tr><th scope="row">When you spend more</th><td data-l="Lead marketplaces">Whenever you want more volume.</td><td data-l="A generalist marketing agency">When the agency recommends it.</td><td data-l="Andrew Ryan Marketing">When the numbers prove it, and after we check the crews can install it.</td></tr>
   <tr><th scope="row">What you keep</th><td data-l="Lead marketplaces">Nothing. Stop paying, the marketing stops.</td><td data-l="A generalist marketing agency">Often not the ad accounts, tracking or data.</td><td data-l="Andrew Ryan Marketing">Your site, ad accounts, data and reporting, from day one.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
 <div class="notyet">
  <div>
   <h3>Sometimes the answer on more marketing is: not yet.</h3>
   <p>If the system isn't producing more than it costs, the math doesn't work, and you deserve to hear that from us first. Sometimes the crews, not the demand, are the limit. We will say so, and show you the math.</p>
   <p><b>Build in the valley, harvest at the peak.</b> Fence searches climb about 20% in March and peak in June and July. Start in the winter and you walk into spring with rankings climbing, reviews collected and campaigns dialed, while competitors who pull back in October hand you the off-season. <a class="tl" href="/pricing/">See every price range <span class="ar">→</span></a></p>
  </div>
  <figure class="season" aria-label="Fence search demand by month: low in winter, rising from March, peaking in June and July, easing in the fall">
   <svg viewBox="0 0 480 190" role="img" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="0" y="0" width="80" height="150" fill="#FDF0EB"/><rect x="400" y="0" width="80" height="150" fill="#FDF0EB"/><text x="40" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#EF662F" letter-spacing="1.5">BUILD</text><text x="440" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#EF662F" letter-spacing="1.5">BUILD</text><path d="M0 128 C40 126, 70 118, 100 100 C140 76, 170 56, 210 40 C235 30, 265 30, 290 42 C320 58, 345 78, 375 96 C410 114, 445 124, 480 127" fill="none" stroke="#EF662F" stroke-width="3"/><text x="250" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#333">Summer peak</text><text x="108" y="84" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#333">March +20%</text><line x1="0" y1="150" x2="480" y2="150" stroke="#E0E0E0"/><g font-size="11" fill="#666" text-anchor="middle"><text x="20" y="170">J</text><text x="60" y="170">F</text><text x="100" y="170">M</text><text x="140" y="170">A</text><text x="180" y="170">M</text><text x="220" y="170">J</text><text x="260" y="170">J</text><text x="300" y="170">A</text><text x="340" y="170">S</text><text x="380" y="170">O</text><text x="420" y="170">N</text><text x="460" y="170">D</text></g></svg>
